However, since your planets have irregular shapes, it would be more complex to implement these algorithms directly. Instead, I suggest using a simpler approach called "rejection sampling" to generate new planets until one is far enough away from the existing ones. Here's an updated version of your `generateRandomPlanets` function:

```typescript
const generateRandomPlanets = (numPlanets, minDistance) => {
  const planets = [];
  let attempts = 0;

  while (planets.length < numPlanets && attempts < 100) {
    attempts++;

    const planet = {
      position: [
        randomPosition(-30, 30),
        randomPosition(-30, 30),
        randomPosition(-30, 30),
